","Stfins inhibit cysteine peptidases by binding to their active sites, preventing the enzyme from cleaving its substrates. These inhibitors are small peptides that mimic the substrate of the enzyme, thereby blocking its function. The inhibitors are often derived from the substrate itself, which enhances their specificity.  

