\[
\text{BSA} = 0.15 \times \sqrt{\text{weight (kg)} \times \text{height (cm)}}
\]
First, convert the patient's weight from pounds to kilograms and height from feet and inches to centimeters.
Weight:
\[
65 \text{ lb} \times 0.453592 \text{ kg/lb} = 29.695 \text{ kg}
\]
