","The neuron doctrine is a fundamental theory in neuroscience that states that the nervous system is composed of individual, independent cells (neurons) that communicate with each other through synapses. This theory states that neurons are the basic structural and functional units of the nervous system, not continuous protoplasmic networks. The debate between Camilio Golgi and Santiago Ramón y Cajy centered on whether neurons were independent cells or interconnected protoplasmic networks, with Cajal's work ultimately supporting the neuron doctrine.",fluency,"# Task Description
