## CONVERSATION

<USER_REQUEST>
If the loading dose of phenytoin in children is 20 mg/kg of body weight to be infused at a rate of 0.5 mg/kg/min, over how many minutes should the dose be administered to a 32-lb. child?
</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
1. Convert the child's weight to kilograms:
   \[
   32 \text{ lb} \times \frac{1 \text{ kg}}{2.2 \text{ lb}} = 14.5 \text{ kg}
   \]

2. Calculate the total loading dose:
   \[
   14.5 \text{ kg} \times 20 \text{ mg/kg} = 290 \text{ mg}
   \]

3. Calculate the infusion time:
   \[
   \frac{290 \text{ mg}}{0.5 \text{ mg/min}} = 580 \text{ min}
   \]

The dose should be administered over \(\boxed{580 \text{ minutes}}\).
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

