The treatment for classical galactosuria is lifelong dietary restriction of galactose, which is a monosaccharide sugar found in milk and other foods. This is because the enzyme galactose-1-phosphate transferase is deficient, leading to the accumulation of galactosuria in the blood and tissues. The goal of treatment is to prevent organ damage and developmental delays.
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

