The standard enthalpy change for a reaction can be calculated using the formula:

ΔH₀ = Σ [ΔH₀(products)] - Σ [ΔH₀(products)]

where ΔH₀ is the standard enthalpy change, and ΔH₀(substance) is the standard enthalpy of formation of the substance.

For the given reaction:

\[
\text{CaO(s)} + \text{H}_2\text{O(l)} \rightarrow \text{Ca(OH)}_2\text{(s)}
