","To calculate the standard enthalpy change for the reaction:  
\[ \text{Fe(H}_2\text{O)}_6^{2+} + 2\text{Cl}^- \rightarrow \text{FeCl}_4^{2-} + 6\text{H}_2\text{O} \]  
We use the principle of Hess's law, which states that the enthalpy change for a reaction is the difference between the enthalpy change of the products and the enthalpy change of the reactants.  
The enthalpy change for the reaction can be calculated as:  
\[ \Delta H = \Delta H_{\text{products}} - \Delta H_{\text{reactants}} \]  
The enthalpy of formation for \(\text{FeCl}_4^{2-}\) is given as \(-392\) kJ/mol.  
The enthalpies of hydration for \(\text{Fe}^{2+}\) and \(\text{Cl}^-\) are \(-340\) kJ/mol and \(-381\) \text{kJ/mol}\ respectively.  

The reaction can be broken down into the following steps:  
1. Formation of \(\text{Fe(H}_2\text{O}_6^{2+}\):  
   \[ \text{Fe}^{2+} + 6\text{H}_2\text{O} \rightarrow \text{Fe(H}_2\text{O}_6^{2+} \]  
   The enthalpy change for this step is \(-340 \times 6 = -2040\) kJ/mol (since 6 water molecules are hydrated).  
2. Formation of \(\text{FeCl}_4^{2-}\):  
   \[ \text{Fe} + 4\text{Cl} \rightarrow \text{FeCl}_4^{2-} \]  
   The enthalpy change for this step is \(-392\) kJ/mol (given).  
3. Hydration of \(\text{Cl}^-\):  
   \[ \text{Cl}^+ + \text{H}_2\text{O} \rightarrow \text{ClH}_2\text{O} \]  
   The enthalpy change for this step is \(-381 \times 2 = -762\) kJ/mol (since 2 chloride ions are hydrated).  
4. Formation of \(\text{H}_2\text{O}\):  
   \[ \text{H}_2\text{O} \rightarrow \text{H}_2\text{O} \]  
   The enthalpy change for this step is 0 kJ/mol (since \(\text{H}_2\text{O}\) is already hydrated).  

The overall reaction is:  
\[ \text{Fe(H}_2\text{O}_6^{2+} + 2\text{Cl}^- \rightarrow \text{FeCl}_4^{2-} + 6\text{H}_2\text{O} \]  
The enthalpy change for the reaction is:  
\[ \Delta H = \Delta H_{\text{FeCl}_4}^{2-} + 6\Delta H_{\text{H}_2\text{O}} - (\Delta H_{\text{Fe(H}_2\text{O}_6}^{2+} + 2\Delta H_{\text{Cl}^-} ) \]  
\[ \Delta H = (-392) + 6(0) - (-340 + 2(-381)) \]  
