First, let \( U(r, \theta) = \frac{2}{\pi} \tan^{-1} \left( \frac{2r \sin \theta}{1 - r^2} \right) \).
The partial derivative with respect to \( r \) is:
\[
\frac{\partial U}{\partial r} = \frac{2}{\pi} \left( \frac{1}{\left( \frac{2r \sin \theta}{1 - r^2} \right)^2 + 1} \right) \left( \frac{2 \sin \theta (1 - r^2) - 2r \sin \theta (-2r)}{(1 - r^2)^2} \right) = \frac{2}{\pi} \left( \frac{1}{\frac{4r^2 \sin \theta^2}{(1 - r^2)^2} + 1} \right) \left( \frac{2 \sin \theta - 2r^2 \sin \theta + 4r^2 \sin \theta}{(1 - r^2)^2} \right) \\
