","To prove that \( B \subseteq A \) if \( A \triangle B \subseteq A \), we can use the definition of the symmetric difference and the properties of symmetric functions.

Given: \( A \triangle B \subseteq A \).
By definition, \( A \triangle B = (A \setminus B) \cup (B \setminus A) \).
