","To calculate the average radiation dose to the liver, we use the formula:
\[
\text{Dose} = \frac{\text{Energy absorbed}}{\text{Mass of tissue}}
\]
where:
- Dose is the radiation dose, typically measured in Grays (Gy).
- Energy absorbed is the energy absorbed by the tissue, measured in Joules (J).
- Mass of tissue is the mass of the tissue, measured in kilograms (kg).

Given:
- Energy absorbed = 0.12 J
- Mass of liver tissue = 1.6 kg

Substituting the given values into the formula:
\[
\text{Dose} = \frac{0.12 \text{ J}}{1.6 \text{ kg}} = 0.075 \text{ Gy}
\]

Thus, the average radiation dose to the liver is \(\boxed{0.075 \text{ Gy}}\).",fluency,"# Task Description
