   K = [ADP][Pi] / [ATP][Pi] = [ADP] / [ATP]  
   Since the concentrations of ATP, ADP, and Pi are all 1 mM, K = 1.  

   Now, substitute the values into the Gibbs free energy equation:  
   ΔG = ΔG° - RT ln(K)  
   ΔG = -30.5 kJ/mol - (8.314 J/mol·K × 314 K) × ln(1)  
   Since ln(1) = 0:  
   ΔG = -30.5 kJ/mol  

