","To calculate the thermal de Broglie wavelength, fugacity, free enthalpy, and entropy for a mole of \(^4\text{He}\) at 1 bar and 290 K, assuming helium behaves as an ideal gas, we can proceed as follows:

1. **Thermal de Broglie wavelength (\(\lambda\))**:  
   The thermal de Broglie wavelength is given by:  
   \[
   \lambda = \frac{h}{\sqrt{2m k_B T}}
   \]  
   where:  
   - \(h\) = Planck’s constant = \(6.624 \times 10^{-34} \text{ J s}\)  
   - \(m\) = mass of \(^4\text{He}\) = \(4 \times 1.66 \times 10^{-27} \text{ g} = 6.64 \times 10^{-27} \text{ g} = 6.64 \times 10^{-27} \text{ kg}\)  
   - \(k_B\) = Boltzmann constant = \(1.36 \times 10^{-23} \text{ J K}^{-1}\)  
   - \(T\) = temperature = \(290 \text{ K}\)  

   Substituting the values:  
   \[
   \lambda = \frac{6.624 \times 10^{-34} \text{ J s}}{\sqrt{2 \times 6.64 \times 10^{-27} \text{ kg} \times 1.36 \times 10^{-23} \text{ J K}^{-1} \times 290 \text{ K}}}
