However, the correct relationship is:  
\[
\lambda_{\text{decay}} = \frac{\lambda}{n_c - n_c}
\]  
where \(n_c\) is the refractive index of the core and \(n_c\) is the refractive index of the cladding.  

Given \(n_{\text{eff}} - n_f = 0.3\), and \(n_{\text{eff}} \approx 1.3\), we have \(n_c > 1.3\).  

For Ga\(_{0.2}\)Al_{0.8}\)As, \(n_c \approx 1.45\).  
For air, \(n_c = 1\).  

Thus, the decay length is:  
\[
\lambda_{\text{decay}} = \frac{\lambda}{n_c - n_c} = \frac{1 \mu\text{m}}{1.45 - 1} = \frac{1 \mu\text{m}}{0.45} \approx 2.13 \mu\text{m}
\]  

