The kinetic molecular theory of gases includes the following postulates:  
1. Gases are composed of particles (atoms or molecules) that move randomly and independently.  
2. The particles of a gas are in constant motion.  
3. The average kinetic energy of the particles is directly proportional to the temperature of the gas.  
4. The gas molecules do not exert forces on each other (no intermolecular forces).  
5. The volume of the gas molecules is negligible compared to the volume of the container.  

